  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting behavioural changes towards gender equality</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CONTRASIDA, founded by Maryknoll sisters, working since 1994 in favor of poor people living with HIV or affected by HIV, is focusing its work in this project in the departments of San Salvador, Sonsonate and La Paz, reaching 141 women and 221 men (362 people) directly, and 1,105 women and 705 men (1,810 people) indirectly in 2014.
The project aims to contribute to generate socio-cultural changes in favor of HIV and gender-based violence prevention  in women and men who participate in Contrasida&apos;s activities (trainings on gender, HIV and Human Rights; radio on-line programme and educational materials), using a human rights approach.</narrative>
  </description>
